# Shell scripts MUST check out with LF endings, on every platform.
#
# Every deploy/*.sh was stored in this repo with CRLF until 2026-08-22 —
# an artefact of being authored on Windows. GNU bash on Ubuntu does not
# reliably tolerate a trailing \r: `set -uo pipefail\r` is an invalid
# option name, and `fi\r` is a syntax error. Git Bash on Windows is
# patched to cope, which is exactly why this went unnoticed here.
#
# These scripts ARE the disaster-recovery path. A recovery is the worst
# moment to discover the recovery script will not parse.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.timer     text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf

# Spreadsheets and archives are binary — never touch their bytes.
*.xlsx      binary
*.xls       binary
*.tar       binary
*.gz        binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.pdf       binary
